# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

/pb_data

# pb_public holds the compiled console, which main.go embeds with
# `//go:embed all:pb_public/*`. A missing directory is a COMPILE error, so a
# fresh clone could not run `go build`, `go vet` or `go test` without first
# installing Node and building the frontend. One placeholder page is tracked so
# the Go side stands alone; `npm run build` overwrites it with the real one
# (vite.config.ts sets emptyOutDir), and that overwrite is not worth committing.
/pb_public/*
!/pb_public/index.html

stone-age
stone-age-authz-test
*.exe

# Claude Code local state: per-machine settings, launch config, and git
# worktrees. worktrees/ in particular holds whole nested working copies of this
# repo -- a trap for anyone grepping the tree, and never something to commit.
.claude/

